    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0842" n="746" xml:id="pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    Hiss Collection</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">United States Delegation Memorandum</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d385-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yalta</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-08">February 8, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">List of Items Referred to Foreign Ministers</hi>
                </p>
                <p>1. Inclusion of Ukraine, White Russia and Lithuania among initial members of the
                    Organization. (See attached paper)</p>
                <p>2. Date and place of United Nations Conference.</p>
                <p>3. Nations to be invited to United Nations Conference.</p>
                <p>Emphasize membership should include all signatories of United Nations
                    Declaration—not just the specific, listed countries which have already
                    signed.</p>
                <p>(See attached list)</p>
                <p>4. The policy toward Iran. (See attached paper)</p>





                <xi:include href="d385-a1.xml" xpointer="d385-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d385-a2.xml" xpointer="d385-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d385-a3.xml" xpointer="d385-a3"/>
                <xi:include href="d385-a4.xml" xpointer="d385-a4"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d385-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d385-f1-content">
                <p>Author not indicated but presumably Hiss.
                    This memorandum, with attachments, was presumably prepared for Stettinius prior to the meeting of the Foreign
                    Ministers on February 8, 1945.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
